Tip 9 - follow these best practices to avoid overlapping elements and ensure proper adaptation of text and numbers, especially during user interactions:
(
    Avoid Overlapping Elements:
Always leave enough padding and margins between chart components (labels, axes, legends, tooltips, titles.
Enable automatic text wrapping or truncation for longer text elements.
Limit the number of data series or chart elements visible at one time if space is limited.

Dynamic Text and Number Adaptation:
Implement responsive design so text and numbers resize or reflow appropriately on different screen sizes and during zoom or filtering.
Use adaptive font sizes, abbreviations (e.g., 1K, 1M), and axis tick formatting to keep numbers readable.
Make sure tooltips and labels reposition dynamically, so they never cover important data points.

Internationalization and Formatting:
Use appropriate number formats for your audience (e.g., decimal and thousand separators).
Ensure all dynamic text (such as legends, labels, and tooltips) adjusts smoothly to various languages and content lengths.

Testing Interactions:
Test all interactions (zoom, filter, resizing) to ensure texts/numbers are not clipped, overlapped, or hidden.
Check chart readability for users with accessibility needs (e.g., color contrast, font size)
)

